# ── Line endings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything textual is LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: `test/contract.mjs` compares the committed client
# artifacts (`lib/client.js`, `packages/molbio-panel/lib/client.js`) with what
# `build/client-bundle-core.mjs` generates from the sources, and the generator
# emits LF. With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) a fresh checkout
# materializes those artifacts with CRLF, so the guard reported "stale" for a
# file whose CONTENT was identical — the false positive that gets a real
# staleness signal ignored. The comparison normalizes line endings too, but the
# repository should not hand out the mismatch in the first place.
#
# One-time consequence of adding this: none for this tree (every tracked text
# file was already LF); a checkout that had CRLF files will see them rewritten.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures: never "normalize" these. `test/fixtures/pUC118.dna` is a real
# SnapGene file, and .ab1 traces are binary too.
*.dna binary
*.ab1 binary
